---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import InterestForm from "../components/InterestForm.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Company formation Andorra | Official constitution steps"
  description="Company formation in Andorra: name reservation, foreign-investment authorisation and a notarial deed, as published on Govern.ad. The official company-tax rate is 10%."
  path="/company-formation"
>
  <section class="page-header">
    <h1>Company formation in Andorra</h1>
    <p>
      Company formation in Andorra is a Government procedure, not a
      package. Non-residents usually need a foreign-investment
      authorisation before a notary can constitute the company.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="prose">
    <div class="notice">
      <p>
        Taken from the Government’s
        <a
          href="https://www.govern.ad/ca/tematiques/empresa-i-emprenedoria/creacio-i-modificacio-d-empreses/punt-empresa/creacio-d-una-empresa-a-andorra"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener">create a company</a
        >
        and
        <a
          href="https://www.govern.ad/ca/tematiques/empresa-i-emprenedoria/creacio-i-modificacio-d-empreses/punt-empresa/fase-de-constitucio-de-la-societat"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener">constitution</a
        >
        pages, and from the
        <a
          href="https://www.e-tramits.ad/tramits/impostos/is"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener">Impost sobre Societats</a
        >
        note on e-tramits.ad. We do not invent gestoria fees. If a figure
        below disagrees with the live page, use the live page.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>What those pages list</h2>
    <p>
      The constitution page lists a NIA, a reserved company name (SL,
      SLU, SA or SAU), a foreign-investment authorisation if you are a
      non-resident, share capital paid into an Andorran bank, a public
      deed before a notary, and Government inscription. The companion
      page adds tax registration, a trade name at the Comú, and
      <a href="/directory/cass">CASS</a>
      if you will employ people. The registered office has to be in
      Andorra.
    </p>
    <p>
      Forming a company is not a residence permit. If you will live here
      and work on your own account, that is still
      <a href="/self-employed-residence">J.1</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Share capital, as published</h2>
    <p>
      The constitution page currently sets minimum share capital at
      <strong>3,000 euros</strong> for an SL and
      <strong>60,000 euros</strong> for an SA, paid into an Andorran
      account with a bank certificate for the notary. Confirm both
      figures on the live page before you treat them as the sum you will
      pay in.
    </p>

    <h2>Company tax</h2>
    <p>
      The official Impost sobre Societats page states that the general
      rate is <strong>10 per cent</strong> for companies that are tax
      resident in Andorra. Special regimes exist. This page does not
      invent reduced rates.
    </p>

    <h2>Counsel</h2>
    <p>
      The official pages expect statutes that match the name-reservation
      and foreign-investment filings. Named firms with their own sites
      are in the
      <a href="/directory">directory</a>.
      Opening the company account is
      <a href="/opening-a-bank-account">a separate note</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <InterestForm
    intro="Leave an email if you want an introduction to counsel for a company file. We’ll write back."
    source="company-formation"
  />
</Base>
